# AN HOUR BEHIND — THE DRIVE, the way home from GOODCO.
#
# The road has TWO scores and they are not a matched pair. OVERDUE is the trip
# out: he is late, the jacket has been answering from the campus for an hour,
# and a clock ticks in every bar of it. This is the trip BACK, and the pressure
# has not come off — it has changed KIND. She was flown off the planet an hour
# before he got through the door. There is no longer a deadline to be late for.
# The thing he was racing has already happened, and she is getting further away
# at the speed of a rocket while he does a hundred and twenty on a town road.
#
# ── IT IS A FIFTY-SECOND PIECE ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# For the reason written out in full at the top of `overdue.song`: a leg of the
# road lasts forty to sixty seconds, and the seventy-six-bar version of this
# score spent its whole back half — the breakdown, the build, the turn — on a
# listener who had already arrived. Thirty-six bars, 49 s, so the fall gets all
# the way to the bottom before the car stops.
#
# The two scores now share a SKELETON and invert everything inside it: the same
# four-bar hinge twice a loop, which CLIMBS chromatically going out and
# ACCELERATES the fall coming home. That is the pairing — one road, two
# directions, one shape, opposite motion.
#
# THREE DECISIONS.
#
#   THE ANSWER IS MISSING. Every phrase in OVERDUE answers itself — a call and
#   a reply, two bars each. Here the call goes out and the reply is a HOLE: two
#   bars of engine, road and kit where a tune used to be. Half the A section is
#   the lead not playing. That is the whole piece.
#
#   AND THE HOLE CLOSES AS THE PIECE RUNS. Two bars of it in A, one in B, none
#   in the TURN — a gradient that was buried inside a ten-section arrangement
#   and is the audible shape of this one. He stops waiting for the reply.
#
#   THE CLOCK IS GONE, AND THAT IS WORSE. The one sound OVERDUE never takes
#   away is deleted here, and what replaces it is a TRACKER PING — one sonar
#   blip, twice in four bars, off the grid, sliding flat as it sounds. It is
#   alone in the first bar of the piece, which is where a short score keeps the
#   thin moment its middle cannot afford, and it is answering from somewhere
#   this car cannot drive to.
#
#   NOTHING EVER CADENCES. The harmony is the oldest falling figure there is —
#   Dm–C–B♭–A, down and down — and it never resolves, not at a section end and
#   not at the loop seam. SLIP is that fall speeding up inside four bars: one
#   chord a half-bar, then two, then four, so by its last bar the descent is
#   happening four times as fast and has still not landed.
#
# Compile:  node scripts/song-import.mjs content/songs/hour_behind.song --sheet

id     hour_behind
title  AN HOUR BEHIND
tempo  176
about
  The road home, and it is not the relief version of OVERDUE — written to the
  same short length, so the fall reaches the bottom before the car stops. He
  has the part on the passenger seat and she left the planet an hour before he
  got through the door, so the deadline has not passed — it has become a
  distance. Every phrase is a call with the reply cut out: two bars of tune,
  two bars of nothing but engine and tarmac where the answer used to be, and
  the hole closes as the piece runs — two bars, then one, then none. The clock
  that runs through the whole of the outbound score is gone, replaced by a
  sonar ping that slides flat as it sounds, twice in four bars, off the grid,
  alone in the opening bar. The harmony falls Dm–C–B♭–A and never once lands,
  and twice a loop a four-bar hinge accelerates that fall to four chords a bar
  rather than climbing out of it — the same hinge the outbound score uses to
  climb. Original melodies; nothing sampled.

# ── THE CAST ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The call. It gets two bars, and then it stops.
voice call   square vol=.03 gate=.75 detune=7 echo=.24 vib=6/12/90
# THE TRACKER. A sonar blip far above everything, bending flat as it rings —
# `slide` is the doppler, and it is the only voice in the score that moves in
# pitch without being told a new note.
voice ping   sine vol=.018 gate=.55 pan=-0.4 echo=.6 slide=.94
# The engine — a lowpassed saw chugging sixteenths, kept up out of the bass.
voice engine sawtooth vol=.016 gate=.45 lp=1500 pan=.25
voice stab   square vol=.012 gate=.2 detune=10 pan=-0.28
voice bass   triangle vol=.056 gate=.8

# ── THE KIT — no tick. There is nothing left to count ──────────────────────
drum kick    triangle vol=.062 gate=1 slide=.25 note=D2
drum snare   noise vol=.035 gate=.72 hp=1500
drum hat     noise vol=.0105 gate=.24 hp=6900 pan=.25

# ── INTRO — the gate, the part on the seat, and the ping already going. This
#    is the score's whole supply of quiet, the same trade OVERDUE makes.
#    NO BAR IN HERE IS COMPLETELY EMPTY: an entirely silent bar engraves as a
#    gap the sheet cannot lay out on its step grid, which is a real fault the
#    notation-geometry guard catches — so the hat comes in under bar two ─────
section intro
  chords Dm | C | Bb | A
  ping   d7*4 .*12 | .*16 | .*9 a6*4 .*3 | .*16
  engine .*16 | .*16 | chug:4 | chug:4
  bass   .*16 | .*16 | gallop:2 | gallop:2
  hat    ................|..x...x...x...x.|x.x.x.x.x.x.x.x.|x.x.x.x.x.x.x.x.

# ── A — call, call, and then two bars of road ─────────────────────────────
section a
  chords Dm | C | Bb | A | Dm | C | Bb | A
  call   d5*2 f5*2 a5*2 d6*2 a5*4 f5*4 | g5*4 e5*4 c5*8 | .*16 | .*16
         d5*2 f5*2 a5*2 d6*2 c6*4 a5*4 | g5*4 e5*4 g5*8 | .*16 | .*16
  ping   d7*4 .*12 | .*16 | .*9 a6*4 .*3 | .*16
  engine chug 4
  stab   offbeat 4
  bass   gallop 2
  kick   x.....x.x.......|x.....x.x.x.....
  snare  ....x.......x...
  hat    x.x.x.x.x.x.x.x.

# ── SLIP — the hinge, and the acceleration and the descent are ONE gesture:
#    the note values halve every bar (half, half, quarter, eighth) while the
#    call falls a whole octave across the four, D6 to A4, and it still does not
#    land. OVERDUE's hinge climbs here; this one drops ───────────────────────
section slip
  chords Dm C | Bb A | Dm C Bb A | Dm C Bb A
  call   d6*8 c6*8 | a#5*8 a5*8
         d5*4 c5*4 a#4*4 a4*4 | d5*2 c5*2 a#4*2 a4*2 d5*2 c5*2 a#4*2 a4*2
  ping   d7*4 .*12 | .*16 | .*9 a6*4 .*3 | .*16
  engine chug 4
  stab   offbeat 4
  bass   drive 2
  kick   x.......x.......|x.......x.......|x.......x...x...|x.......x...x...
  snare  ....x.......x...|....x.......x.x.|....x...x.x.x.x.|x.x.x.x.x.x.x.x.
  hat    x.x.x.x.x.x.x.x.

# ── B — it almost answers itself. One bar of hole instead of two ──────────
section b
  chords Dm | C | Bb | A | Dm | C | Bb | A
  call   a5*2 d6*2 f6*4 e6*2 d6*2 c6*2 a5*2 | g5*2 c6*2 e6*4 d6*4 c6*4 | a#5*2 d6*2 f6*4 d6*4 a#5*4 | .*16
         d6*4 f6*4 d6*4 a5*4 | c6*4 e6*4 g5*8 | a#5*4 d6*4 f6*8 | .*16
  ping   d7*4 .*12 | .*16 | .*9 a6*4 .*3 | .*16
  engine chug 4
  stab   offbeat 4
  bass   gallop 2
  kick   x.....x.x.......|x.....x.x.x.....
  snare  ....x.......x...
  hat    x.x.x.x.x.x.x.x.

# ── TURN — the widest the call gets, no hole left in it at all, and it is
#    cut off mid-phrase ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
section turn
  chords Dm | C | Bb | A | Dm | C | Bb | A
  call   d6*2 c6*2 a#5*2 a5*2 f5*4 d5*4 | e5*2 g5*2 c6*4 e6*4 g5*4 | f6*4 d6*4 a#5*8 | c#6*4 e6*4 a5*8
         d6*2 f6*2 a6*4 f6*4 d6*4 | c6*4 g5*4 e5*8 | a#5*2 d6*2 f6*4 d6*8 | c#6*4 e6*4 .*8
  ping   d7*4 .*12 | .*16 | .*9 a6*4 .*3 | .*16
  engine chug 4
  stab   stab 4
  bass   gallop 2
  kick   x.....x.x.......|x.....x.x.x.....
  snare  ....x.......x...|....x.......x.x.
  hat    x.x.x.x.x.x.x.x.

order  intro a slip b slip turn
